# Line endings are part of the content here, not a platform preference.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks out text files with CRLF, and every
# golden-file comparison fails on that leg alone -- nine of them in
# internal/supervisor did, reporting "the prompt changed under an empty
# toolkit config" when nothing about the prompt had changed (OR-340).
#
# Shell scripts are worse than a failed assertion: bash rejects a script whose
# shebang line ends in CR, so a CRLF checkout of scripts/test.sh breaks the
# Windows CI leg itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must never touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
